    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Measles is a <strong>highly contagious</strong> viral disease spread through inhaling droplets from coughs or sneezes of infected people. Symptoms include a high fever and red, blotchy rash. Measles can lead to serious complications such as <em>pneumonia</em> or brain damage. It is preventable by the <strong>MMR vaccine</strong> which protects against measles, mumps, and rubella.</p>",
